# NEXUS FINANCE CONSTITUTION LAYER

## Overview

The `constitution/` directory contains public-facing materials related to the constitutional and invariant-oriented layer of the NEXUS Finance contracts repository.

This layer exists to express protocol discipline through explicit invariant logic, registry-backed references, and constitution-oriented structure at the contract and documentation level.

## Why This Layer Exists

NEXUS Finance is being developed with a governance-aware and audit-oriented design posture.

The constitution layer exists to support:

- explicit invariant definition
- structured protocol discipline
- registry-backed referenceability
- stronger long-term architectural coherence

Its purpose is to reduce ambiguity around critical protocol principles and to reinforce interpretable system boundaries.

## What the Constitution Layer Contains

The public constitution layer currently includes materials such as:

- constitution-related contract logic
- constitution invariant documentation
- constitution registry references

These materials should be understood as part of the broader protocol discipline framework rather than as isolated experimental artifacts.

## Review Role

The constitution layer is intended to support higher-order technical interpretation of the protocol.

It complements:

- the core contracts in `src/`
- the public architecture and risk documentation in `docs/`
- governance-related review materials
- deployment and registry evidence

It is not intended to replace direct source code review or broader protocol evaluation.

## Public Scope and Limits

This layer is public-facing and explanatory in role.

It does not claim to expose every broader internal governance process, every economic modeling component, or every protocol-adjacent design layer associated with the wider NEXUS Finance system.

Its function is to make the constitutional and invariant-oriented layer of the public contracts repository more interpretable.

## Summary

The `constitution/` directory is a public constitutional and invariant-oriented layer intended to support protocol discipline, reviewer understanding, and long-term architectural clarity within the NEXUS Finance contracts repository.
